ull,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced on a store copy after humdrum-priestly-lcont merged: 3 ids = 3 whole-store passes, 29,238 reductions, peak 44.8 MB (1 id = 1 pass, 9,746). Plan revised: the repeat is build_dep_graph's per-id cache miss reloading the whole store; per-id fields already come from a single-directory reduce in show_state, so original plan item 2 needs no change. The fix shares one memoised states loader across the ids.","timestamp":1793317822819755001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Measured on a store copy (9,746 entries), graph cache deleted before each run, summary of 3 ids (d70a-97d9, d40f-1154, 0076-375d): before (origin/main 6acef632) 3 whole-store passes, 29,238 ticket reductions, tracemalloc peak 44.8 MB; after 1 pass, 9,746 reductions, peak 47.1 MB (the shared states stay alive across the ids, about 2 MB more). Output JSON-equal. All 3 sampled ids read 'ready' on the copy; the blocked path is covered by the fixture test (blocked, ready, unblocked-by-closed, archived, session_log, unknown ids, equal to the per-id loop).","timestamp":1793318532454484001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on b6821fd4314: lint, typecheck, import-convention guard green; 19,841 passed, 88 skipped, 0 failed.","timestamp":1793321347866609001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793301714617550001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"80310d58-2bec-436c-8e69-150483d8aab5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"dff5-6fe2-646c-4a0e"},{"link_uuid":"73abfc80-2969-407a-8666-79e4d08bee0a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a64d-328d-7c70-499a"}],"description":"## Observation\n\nThe `summary` read (src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py, around line 480) calls `deps_state` once per requested id, and each call can rebuild the dependency graph from a full whole-store reduce. Measured on a clone of the live store, 2026-10-29: 3 ids took 29,187 ticket reductions and read 935 MB from disk, with a peak of 284.4 MB per pass.\n\nRe-measured on a fresh copy after humdrum-priestly-lcont merged (6acef632), graph cache removed before each run: 3 ids took 3 whole-store passes and 29,238 ticket reductions (1 id: 1 pass, 9,746), peak 44.8 MB (the trimmed graph load). The repeat comes from `build_dep_graph` (src/rebar/graph/_graph.py): its cache stores graphs per ticket id, so each new id misses and `_compute_dep_graph` calls `load_indexed_states` again. Nothing a summary does changes ticket directories between ids (the graph load uses `exclude_archived=False`, so it heals no markers; only `.graph-cache.json` is written, which the load skips as a dot-file), so the states are the same for every id.\n\nPlan item 2 of the original plan is already true: the per-id fields come from `show_state` without the inbound scan, which reduces only the named ticket directory. It needs no change.\n\n## Plan\n1. Give `build_dep_graph` and `_compute_dep_graph` an optional keyword-only `load_states` callable (internal; `build_dep_graph` is not in the public API surface). When given, a cache miss calls it instead of `load_indexed_states`; a cache hit never calls it.\n2. Thread it through `reads.deps_state` (same optional keyword) and add `gates.summary_many(ticket_ids, tracker)`, which builds one memoised loader (loads at most once, and only if some id misses the cache) and calls `summary_compute(..., load_states=...)` per id. `summary_cli` and the library `rebar.summary` (src/rebar/_lib_gates.py) call `summary_many`; `rebar.summary`'s signature is unchanged.\n3. Tests first, seen failing on current code: with 3 ids and no graph cache, `summary_many` performs exactly one `reduce_all_tickets` call; its output equals the per-id `summary_compute` loop on a multi-id fixture (blocked, ready, archived, unknown and session_log ids); with a warm cache it performs none.\n4. Measure passes, reductions and tracemalloc peak for 3 ids on a store copy before and after, compare outputs, and record them here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] `summary` with 3 ids and no graph cache performs 1 `reduce_all_tickets` call, not 3; verified by a counting test in tests/unit/test_summary_single_graph_load.py and on a store copy.\n- [x] `summary` output for a multi-id fixture equals the per-id loop's output; verified by the same test module.\n- [x] Before/after passes, reductions, peak and output equality on a store copy are recorded in a ticket comment.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py\n- src/rebar/graph/_graph.py\n- src/rebar/_lib_gates.py\n- tests/unit/test_summary_single_graph_load.py","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py","reason":"summary_many shares one graph load"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"deps_state forwards load_states"},{"path":"src/rebar/graph/_graph.py","reason":"build_dep_graph accepts a states loader"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_gates.py","reason":"rebar.summary calls summary_many"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_summary_single_graph_load.py","reason":"single-pass and output-equality tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","a64d-328d-7c70-499a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"40b28643-c7e7-4969-98e1-8e76991a629e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d40f-1154-61d4-4f13","ticket_type":"bug","title":"summary reduces the whole store once per ticket id","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c3eaafad-aa91-44f5-b690-f0494c711605","15f3380a-c600-422d-8bcf-8044caa16d3e","dd89e4e8-9cbe-4b37-8395-9c74acde00b0","bd64203b-79db-4c5e-9ad0-7817764b9244","cc0f96a3-5b2f-45db-8df7-df273f5ae94d","79524f5b-f1d1-44e5-a1a5-00a079e06851","ab5700b8-6a75-4bda-bab5-aa11b44dbe5b","32a4e807-792a-48d5-8ff6-0abd96622d0b","73abfc80-2969-407a-8666-79e4d08bee0a","15901b4e-1f7c-4699-ab32-fcb976f900a1","40b28643-c7e7-4969-98e1-8e76991a629e","5eb201cc-602c-4858-aaad-dcc7a8d6776b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793340961202640799,"uuid":"ad182174-da8e-462d-a2ee-133bc844b30b"}